Fix a double free when DUMB cannot open the in-memory file.

dumbfile_mem_status deletes its buffer in its destructor, so the explicit
delete[] on the dumbfile_open_ex() failure path freed it twice.

Upstream: generic bug, suitable for xbmc/audiodecoder.dumb.

--- a/src/DumbCodec.cpp
+++ b/src/DumbCodec.cpp
@@ -126,7 +126,7 @@
   DUMBFILE* f = dumbfile_open_ex(&memdata, &mem_dfs);
   if (!f)
   {
-    delete[] memdata.ptr;
+    // memdata's destructor releases ptr.
     return false;
   }
 
